          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "The bow was often kept in a case made of leather or of cloth. To make it “naked” meant to take it out of its case in order to use it. The expression signifies a preparation for war, and is of the same meaning as “uncovering the shield.” See note on Isaiah 22:6 (#500)."
      }
